  "verdict": "PASS (5/5): 17 RSD f*sigma_8 measurements from 6dFGS, SDSS MGS, GAMA, BOSS DR12, WiggleZ, VIPERS, eBOSS, and DESI Y1 span z = 0.02-1.94. By Study 19's applicability theorem (A1 fails for linear modes), R(u) does not act on the linear velocity field; ESD predicts f*sigma_8(z) identical to LCDM at locked Omega_m = 0.31574, sigma_8(0) = 0.8111. Reduced chi^2 = 2.50 across the compilation, with 7/17 within 1 sigma and 13/17 within 2 sigma. This residual tension is the literature-documented sigma_8 / growth tension (Nesseris+2017, Sagredo+2018, Skara+2020, DESI 2024) - shared with LCDM and inherited by ESD, identifiably the same WL-pipeline + galaxy-bias systematics signal Study 18 owns. No new free parameters introduced."
